ed-graft-arm64.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":626,"digest":"sha256:10632f4294b8e813902302622c954a23ccc3d529dbd6caeb2a5421522ecfc0e2","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-06T19:01:05Z","updated_at":"2026-11-06T19:01:05Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/ivo-lopes/ivoai/releases/download/v0.17.0/managed-graft-arm64.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ivo-lopes/ivoai/tarball/v0.17.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ivo-lopes/ivoai/zipball/v0.17.0","body":"# IVOAI v0.17.0 — backend-first native execution and administration\n\n## User-visible changes\n\n- Managed Codex accepts natural requests through the Core. The opt-in adaptive\n  Primary answers simple requests without a DAG and uses the existing planning,\n  approval and worker protocol when a task needs them. Native exit, multiple\n  turns and eligible cross-process resume retain admission and NoReplay checks.\n- Official Codex 0.167.0 and its exact companion are reviewed alongside the\n  previously certified 0.166.0 and 0.162.1 pairs. Adaptive certification remains\n  Linux amd64 with exact hashes; the feature is not globally enabled.\n- The optional native read-only Code Intelligence Gateway reuses exact evidence,\n  invalidates changed sources and checks authorization on cache hits and recovery.\n  Enable it only through its documented experimental flag. Admitted native\n  turns with authoritative evidence carry the existing EXACT fidelity contract\n  to the runner and bypass lossy proxies. Requested/default Caveman stays stored;\n  the effective Direct/bypass event reports the actual decision consistently.\n- The administrative web console uses the same backend, with authentication,\n  authorization, explicit mutation confirmations, audit, sanitized bounded output,\n  revocation/logout and reverse-proxy/TLS publication. It adds no chat frontend.\n- Optional Antigravity 1.5.2 headless execution shares Core admission, sessions,\n  tools and workers. Real official two-turn, permission-denial and approved DAG\n  integrations passed. This does not claim transparent native TUI control.\n  The reviewed executable requires PCLMULQDQ. Startup passed on emulated CPUs\n  with that feature and AVX/AVX2 disabled; an incompatible CPU is now rejected\n  before client discovery, lease creation or an execution attempt.\n- Optional Claude headless integration uses the official supported interface and\n  the same Core. Protocol checks use an isolated synthetic provider; real Claude\n  subscription inference remains pending because the user has no account.\n- Real private Context ingestion now completes document import, semantic search\n  and exact recovery. Synchronous Qdrant mutations encode `wait=true` correctly,\n  preserve proxy parameters and do not retry mutations. Only cold collection\n  creation receives a bounded 60-second budget; stricter clients and caller\n  cancellation still win. Shared Mindsite synchronization remains pending.\n- Managed TEI suppresses its credential-bearing INFO argument record through\n  the supported `LOG_LEVEL` target filter. Raw runtime logs were checked before\n  sanitization: the key was absent while health, metrics, authentication,\n  embeddings and error diagnostics remained functional. Earlier logs are retained;\n  no credential is rotated automatically.\n- Managed OpenCode installation, repair, probing and execution are removed.\n  `ivoai auto` enters managed Codex. Old entry points return explicit migration\n  errors. Existing personal binaries, configurations, credentials and histories\n  are retained; legacy wire contracts remain readable.\n\n## Dependencies and recoverability\n\nReviewed runtime and JavaScript locks are refreshed, including ai-memory 3.4.2,\nQdrant 1.20.0, Headroom 0.43.1, Ruflo 3.72.2, pnpm 12.18.0 and Playwright 1.65.0.\nPython remains 3.14.10, the latest compatible reviewed runtime: the 3.15.2 probe\nfailed on a required PyYAML wheel and is preserved as an unsupported combination.\nUnchanged dependencies retain their verified pins rather than being repinned\nwithout a version change.\n\n`UV_OFFLINE=1` explicitly allows Headroom installation/reapplication from its\nreviewed cache while retaining the isolated environment, wheel hashes, constraints\nand forced installation. Missing cache fails without publishing a launcher.\nThe complete stable-upgrade gate uses this mode only in its network-isolated\nphase; cache preparation remains online. The initial unsuccessful reapplication\nand the successful focused/cache-miss reproductions are retained as evidence.\n\nCaveman 4.0.2-ivoai.1 is an IVOAI Apache-2.0 rebuild of reviewed upstream source\nwith repaired Go dependencies. Both rebuilt binaries passed vulnerability scans;\nupstream vulnerable executables are not installed as a fallback. Source, patches,\narchive identity and notices are bound into release metadata. This local rebuild\nis not an upstream signature. Caveman stays the default when eligible, Headroom\noptional and Direct the explicit safe fallback; authoritative memory/context\nbypass destructive compression.\n\nServer dependency migration requires stopped services, private snapshots of data\nand index, isolated old/new validation and explicit activation. Rollback restores\nMemory into an empty tree and preserves forward-only files in quarantine. A real\nprivate Memory2.6.3→3.4.2→2.6.3/Qdrant1.19.2→1.20→1.19.2 cycle passed, including\nexact restored names/hashes before restart. Memory, index and config activation\nare not one atomic transaction: an interrupted later step can require manual\nrecovery with services stopped and snapshots/quarantines retained. Production\nsystemd and resource-limit enforcement are separate operator validations.\n\nUse the retained previous Core/profile and the original verified v0.16.0 assets\nfor rollback. Historical tags, asset bytes and benchmark outcomes are unchanged.\nThe current twelve-file bundle replaces the former OpenCode assets with the\nreviewed Caveman archives and metadata; the old bundle verifier remains separate.\n\n## Validation and limits\n\nSource-bound evidence covers official Codex DAG/resume and the integrated\nthree-turn public Gateway flow, plus a separate real cached-receipt revocation\nflow. The latter denies presentation/recovery after owner revocation even when\nnative inference completes; duplicates create no new attempt. Administrative\nbrowser checks include actual local OAuth/Store and TLS proxy flows. Native CPU\nstartup/emulation, real installers, negative artifact controls, Go tests/race,\nvulnerability scans, migration and rollback gates retain their own scopes.\nEmulated startup does not certify native ARM inference or adaptive ARM sessions.\n\nBoth unfavorable and passing attempts remain recorded. A rejected live admission\nor skipped opt-in test is not counted as successful inference. The release\nworkflow requires native AMD/ARM builds, exact final-bundle upgrade/rollback and\nlocal plus downloaded draft-asset verification before publication.\n\n**Global economic gate: INCOMPLETE.** The separate 54-attempt cohort contains two\nfailures and worse input/time in its comparable subset; no aggregate savings are\nclaimed. Cache hits and smaller tool output are not billed-session savings.\n\nMindsite Context synchronization remains BLOCKED under IVOAI-175 until an\noperator-fed ingestion and retrieval are proved for that shared service. Agent\nsessions keep Context read-only. Private Context certification does not imply\nshared-service synchronization. Optional providers and unproved client parity\nremain feature-flagged; no paid API fallback or subscription credential copying\nis introduced.\n"}